ible. 3.."}, "syn_report": "Question: A post-mortem lung examination of a 68-year-old male overweight male with evidence of chronic lower extremity edema, a 60 pack-year smoking history and daily productive cough would be most likely to reveal: \nOptions: {'A': 'Keratin pearls', 'B': 'Reid Index > 50%', 'C': 'Hypereosinophilia', 'D': 'Non-caseating granulomas', 'E': 'Evidence of a necrotizing infection'} \nTotal Analysis: The post-mortem lung examination of the 68-year-old male with a significant smoking history and chronic symptoms is most likely to reveal chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), specifically chronic bronchitis and emphysema, and possibly pulmonary hypertension. The chronic bronchitis is indicated by the daily productive cough, while the smoking history and age suggest severe emphysema, potentially evidenced by a Reid Index > 50%. The chronic lower extremity edema points towards right-sided heart failure, likely secondary to pulmonary hypertension. The presence of keratin pearls, hypereosinophilia, non-caseating granulomas, and evidence of a necrotizing infection are not expected findings in this context, thus they can be ruled out. The comprehensive analysis aligns with the multidisciplinary perspectives from pulmonology, pathology, cardiology, internal medicine, and geriatrics, confirming the primary diagnosis of COPD and its associated complications.''' \n", "vote_history": [{"Pulmonology": "yes", "Pathology": "yes", "Cardiology": "yes", "Internal Medicine": "yes", "Geriatrics": "yes"}], "revision_history": [], "syn_repo_history": ["Question: A post-mortem lung examination of a 68-year-old male overweight male with evidence of chronic lower extremity edema, a 60 pack-year smoking history and daily productive cough would be most likely to reveal: \nOptions: {'A': 'Keratin pearls', 'B': 'Reid Index > 50%', 'C': 'Hypereosinophilia', 'D': 'Non-caseating granulomas', 'E': 'Evidence of a necrotizing infection'} \nTotal Analysis: The post-mortem l